# CSA CLI Audit â€” brain/cli + hace/cli
## Trieu chung (Reported symptoms)

```
hace brain prompt "hello"           â†’ tokens (ASCII placeholder)  â€” WRONG
hace brain model verify model.gguf  â†’ stub output                 â€” WRONG
hace brain replay save session.sio  â†’ stub output                 â€” WRONG
-bash: syntax error near unexpected token `('                     â€” SHELL BUG
hace brain --model  --prompt        â†’ max_tokens: 64 (empty args) â€” WRONG
hace brain --model  --prompt        â†’ max_tokens: 64 (same again) â€” SAME OUTPUT
```

**Root cause summary: 3 independent bugs, not 1.**

---

## BUG-1 | All commands same output â€” DISPATCH VOID

```yaml
root_cause: "brain/cli/src/executor.rs routes moi subcommand toi cung 1 stub"
evidence:
  - "brain/runtime/src/bridges/hacedle.rs::execute_inference() = prompt.bytes().map(|b| b as u32)"
  - "BrainMasterRuntime.execute() = Ok(SioOutcome::default()) â€” tra ve ngay"
  - "CandleProvider.execute() = Ok(SioOutcome::default())"
  - "LlamaProvider.execute() = Ok(SioOutcome::default())"
dispatch_chain_actual: |
  hace brain prompt "hello"
    -> brain::BrainCmd::dispatch()
    -> executor::BrainExecutor::run()
    -> BrainMasterRuntime::execute()   <- tat ca subcommands deu vao day
    -> SioOutcome::default()           <- tra ve rong
    -> print tokens/stub               <- output giong nhau

dispatch_chain_expected: |
  hace brain prompt "hello"
    -> PromptCmd::run(prompt="hello", model=cfg)
    -> ZeusRuntime::execute(ReasonCtx { action="hello" })
    -> AlgoParticle::reason() hoac HacedleBrain::reason()
    -> print ReasonResult.output

  hace brain model verify model.gguf
    -> ModelCmd::verify(path="model.gguf")
    -> TensorResolver::load_gguf(path)
    -> print metadata: layers, tensors, quant_type

  hace brain replay save session.sio
    -> ReplayCmd::save(path="session.sio")
    -> SessionStore::save(path)
    -> print "saved: session.sio"
```

---

## BUG-2 | `-bash: syntax error near unexpected token '('`

```yaml
root_cause: "Shell tries to execute hace as shell function/alias, not binary"
mechanism: |
  Khi 'hace' khong phai la binary trong PATH ma la:
  - Shell function co syntax error: function hace() { ... ( ... } <- loi ngoac
  - Hoac: alias hace='...(...)...' <- bash reject
  - Hoac: hace binary chua build/install, bash fall-through to eval output
    va output chua '(' (e.g. "AlgoParticle { ... }" )

most_likely: |
  brain/scripts/ hoac hace/cli/build_msvc.bat chua shell function
  hoac hace binary chua duoc 'cargo install' vao PATH.
  User chay 'hace brain ...' trong bash nhung hace la Windows .exe
  khong executable trong bash/WSL context.

diagnosis: |
  'hace' binary la Windows PE (.exe), khong phai ELF.
  Neu chay trong Git Bash / WSL: chua duoc build cho Linux target.
  Neu chay trong PowerShell: nen dung hace.exe hoac cargo run --bin hace.

fix: "Xem PATCH-3 ben duoi"
```

---

## BUG-3 | `--model  --prompt` empty values + `max_tokens: 64` always

```yaml
root_cause: "Arg parser khong read value sau flag â€” hoac print debug format thay output"
evidence:
  - "hace brain --model  --prompt (no values after flags)"
  - "max_tokens: 64 xuat hien tren dong rieng â€” debug print, khong phai real output"
mechanism: |
  brain/cli/src/command.rs dinh nghia arg parsing.
  Neu dung clap: `--model <MODEL>` nhung thieu <MODEL> placeholder
  hoac takes_value(true) chua set -> value bi parse thanh next flag.
  
  "max_tokens: 64" la debug print tu BrainExecutor hoac BrainCmd::run():
    println!("max_tokens: {}", self.max_tokens);
  
  Tat ca commands print cung debug format vi dispatch void (BUG-1).

fix: "Xem PATCH-1 ben duoi"
```

